      "description": "Finds the checked facts that apply to a question, with their sources. Call get_facts before answering a question about company data. Pass structured metrics, dimension_filters and inclusive UTC dates when known. Without window, the dates in the question are read (such as 2026, last quarter or 1 Jan to 30 Sep) and dates_read says how; without any dates, the question is read at today and assumed_date says so. The member names you just queried in the data tool work as names, and a name that isn't known comes back with the closest that is. A dimension filter with no values names the dimension for every value, as in a breakdown by market. Returns the checked facts (items) that apply, with their sources, coverage and links, and the domain of each asked metric; with response_format concise, a short reply without bodies, evidence and links. A link neither widens where a fact applies nor proves a cause. Read a linked fact with read_item only when it helps answer the question.",
