      "description": "Finds facts by the words people use, such as GMV or Spain, and what each metric means. Call get_facts before answering a question about company data. Find what is written down about a few words or a question, by the names people use: metrics and their other names (such as GMV), markets, domains, member names from the data tool (such as payments.orders), and words in a fact. Use it for "what do we know about", "what is" or "how is it defined", and when you don't know the exact names. Returns the matching facts (items) with titles and summaries, and for each metric or dimension the words name: the definition its source gives, where that definition comes from, and what these facts add. When no words match, it returns the facts that apply to what the words name, on the dates the window or the words give (dates_read says how it read the words) or else today, as assumed_date says; when nothing is found, why says what to try. Read a fact in full with read_item.",
